From 629fbb786cc40a3f12b072784bcc53e16bd4d4ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: airidosas252 <airidaslideikis@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:32:55 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 08/20] tu/kgsl: Split bind ranges on sparse unbind

KGSL_GPUMEM_RANGE_OP_UNBIND removes every VBO bind range it overlaps, as
a whole. It does not split them, while BIND does. Applications such as
vkd3d-proton merge consecutive tiles into one bind, so unbinding a single
tile also unmapped its neighbours.

Track bound ranges per sparse VMA in an rb_tree:
 - On unbind, unbind each overlapped range completely, then re-bind the
   parts outside the requested range.
 - Release BO references only after the submit ioctl. The kernel looks up
   child ids while it prepares the ranges.

VK-CTS on Adreno 840 (KGSL), unchanged before/after except where noted:
  dEQP-VK.sparse_resources.buffer.*               142 pass, 0 fail, 99 not supported
    (+8 ResourceError, capture_replay only)
  dEQP-VK.sparse_resources.queue_bind.*            17 pass, 0 fail,  1 not supported
  dEQP-VK.sparse_resources.image_sparse_residency.*  2772 / 0 / 1503
  dEQP-VK.sparse_resources.image_sparse_binding.*    1977 / 0 / 768
  dEQP-VK.sparse_resources.image_sparse_memory_aliasing.*  480 / 0 / 368
  dEQP-VK.sparse_resources.image_rebind.*             256 / 0 / 224
  dEQP-VK.sparse_resources.mipmap_sparse_residency.*  360 / 0 / 300
The CTS does not unbind single tiles out of a larger bind. A standalone test
(6 GiB sparse buffer, random bind/unbind churn) failed with 97683 of 381717
tile checks reading zero before, and 0 after.
